--TEST--
inside a string literal at a `propertyPath<T>` parameter, each `.` after a valid prefix offers the public properties of the class that prefix reaches, read off the rosters the checker recorded — `rule:ide/a-field-path-completes-one-segment-at-a-time`
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Address {
    public string $city = "Bern";
    private string $code = "3000";
}
class Customer {
    public string $name = "Ada";
    public ?Address $address = null;
}
class Order {
    public string $id = "o1";
    public ?Customer $customer = null;
}
class Grid {
    public static function sortBy(propertyPath<Order> $column): string {
        return $column as string;
    }
}

echo Grid::sortBy("customer.address.<|>");
--REQUEST--
completion
--EXPECT--
city    property  string
